    <item>
      <title>The Birthday Paradox in Production: When Random IDs Collide</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/posts/birthday-paradox/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 28 Nov 2025 06:00:00 -0700</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/birthday-paradox/</guid>
      <description>&lt;figure style=&#34;margin: 0 20px 10px 20px; text-align: center;&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;a href=&#34;http://localhost:1313/posts/birthday-paradox/birthday-paradox.png&#34; class=&#34;lightbox-trigger&#34; aria-label=&#34;Open full-size image&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;        &lt;img src=&#34;http://localhost:1313/posts/birthday-paradox/birthday-paradox.png&#34; alt=&#34;&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;    &lt;figcaption style=&#34;font-size: 0.9em; color: #555; margin-top: 5px;&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;        &lt;em&gt;With just 23 random selections from 365 options, you have a 50% chance of collision. Now imagine billions of UUIDs.&lt;/em&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/figure&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;You generate a &lt;a class=&#34;glossary-term&#34; href=&#34;http://localhost:1313/glossary/#uuid-v4&#34; data-definition=&#34;A 128-bit UUID format in which 122 bits are randomly generated, providing an extremely large space of possible identifiers.&#34;&gt;UUID&lt;/a&gt;. It&amp;rsquo;s 128 bits total, with 122 bits of randomness. That&amp;rsquo;s 340 undecillion possible values. Collision-proof, right? Your system generates a million IDs per second. Still safe? What about a billion?&lt;/p&gt;</description>
